.TH CLI-TOOLS 1 "26 October 2026" "cli-tools 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cli-tools \- everyday command-line utilities: paths, system, network, files and disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cli-tools
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B man cli-tools
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cli-tools
is a set of small utilities with matching Linux (bash), PowerShell and Windows Command Prompt
versions. Each tool has the same name and purpose on every platform. Running
.B cli-tools
with no arguments, or with
.B \-h
or
.BR \-\-help ,
prints a summary of every tool. This page documents the Linux versions.
.PP
Per-tool notes are installed as
.I docs/<tool>.md
under
.I ~/.local/share/cli-tools
(user install) or
.I /usr/local/share/cli-tools
(system install).
.SH PATHS AND COMMANDS
.TP
.B pathlist
Print each PATH entry on its own line, flagging missing folders and duplicate entries.
.TP
.BI whichall " NAME " "" [ NAME ...]
Every executable on PATH matching each
.IR NAME ,
in search order; the first one listed is the one that runs. Exits 1 if a name is not found.
.TP
.B refreshenv
Reload PATH into the current bash session from a fresh login shell, picking up changes
installers made to
.I /etc/profile.d
and
.IR ~/.profile .
.B refreshenv
is a shell function set up by the installer; without it, run
.BR "source refreshenv.sh" .
.SH SYSTEM
.TP
.B sysinfo
One-screen summary of host, OS, model, serial, uptime, CPU, memory and disks.
.TP
.B pendingreboot
Report whether a reboot is pending, and why
.RI ( /var/run/reboot-required ,
.BR needs-restarting ).
Exits 0 if not, 2 if a reboot is pending.
.TP
.B mdmstatus
Intune status on Linux: the Microsoft Intune app and identity broker services.
Exits 0 if the Intune app is present, 2 if it is not installed.
.TP
.BR eventerrors " [\fIHOURS\fR] [\fIMAX\fR] [" \-w | \-\-warnings ]
Recent critical and error log entries from
.BR journalctl ,
or syslog when journald is not available. Run with
.B sudo
to include system-wide entries.
.RS
.TP
.I HOURS
How far back to look (default 24).
.TP
.I MAX
Most entries to show (default 50).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-warnings
Include warnings too.
.RE
.SH NETWORK
.TP
.BR netinfo " [" \-p | \-\-public ]
Addresses, default gateway and DNS servers.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-public
Also look up the public IP via https://api.ipify.org (one external request; needs
.BR curl ).
.RE
.TP
.BI portcheck " HOST PORT " "" [ TIMEOUT ]
Test whether a remote TCP port is reachable.
.I TIMEOUT
is in seconds (default 3). Exits 0 if open, 2 if closed or filtered.
.TP
.BI portowner " PORT"
Show which process is listening on (or using) a local port. Exits 2 if nothing is using it.
Run with
.B sudo
to see other users' processes.
.TP
.BI certcheck " HOST " "" [ PORT ] " " [ WARN_DAYS ]
TLS certificate subject, issuer, expiry and trust for a host (needs
.BR openssl ).
.I PORT
defaults to 443;
.I WARN_DAYS
(default 30) flags certificates expiring within that many days. Exits 0 if valid, 2 if
expired, expiring soon or untrusted, 1 on error.
.TP
.BI dnscheck " NAME " "" [ TYPE ] " " [ SERVER ...]
Resolve
.I NAME
with the system resolver and other DNS servers side by side. Exits 2 if the answers differ
(normal for CDNs). Works best with
.B dig
installed.
.RS
.TP
.I TYPE
A (default), AAAA, CNAME, MX, TXT, NS, SRV, SOA or PTR.
.TP
.I SERVER
Servers to compare against (default 1.1.1.1 and 8.8.8.8);
.B none
for the system resolver only. Public servers see the name you look up.
.RE
.SH FILES AND DISK
.TP
.BR dirsize " [\fIPATH\fR] [\fITOP\fR]"
Largest immediate subfolders of
.I PATH
(default: current directory), staying on one filesystem.
.I TOP
is how many to list (default 15).
.TP
.BR bigfiles " [\fIPATH\fR] [\fITOP\fR]"
Largest files under
.I PATH
(default: current directory), staying on one filesystem.
.I TOP
is how many to list (default 20).
.TP
.BR hashfile " [" "\-a sha256" | sha1 | md5 | sha512 "] \fIFILE\fR [\fIFILE\fR ...]"
Hash of each file (default sha256).
.TP
.BR dupfiles " [\fIPATH\fR] [\fIMIN_SIZE_KB\fR]"
Find duplicate files (same size, then same SHA256) under
.IR PATH .
Reports only; deletes nothing. Files smaller than
.I MIN_SIZE_KB
(default 1) are ignored. Exits 2 if duplicates are found.
.TP
.BR syncsafe " [\fIPATH\fR] [" \-\-max " \fIN\fR] [" \-\-win\-root " \fIPREFIX\fR]"
Find names that break Windows or cloud sync: long paths, invalid characters, trailing
spaces or dots, reserved names (CON, NUL, COM1 ...) and names over 255 characters.
Exits 2 if any are found.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-max " N"
Path length to flag, 100 or more (default 260, the Windows MAX_PATH limit).
.TP
.BI \-\-win\-root " PREFIX"
Measure lengths as if
.I PATH
were mounted at this Windows path, for example
.BR "\-\-win\-root 'X:\e\eGoogleDrive\e\eShared'" .
.RE
.TP
.BR empty\-directories " [\fIoptions\fR] \fIINPUT_FILE\fR"
Empty (and by default remove) every directory listed in a .txt or .csv file: one path per
line or a comma-separated list, with an optional
.B base: /path
line. Every entry is listed first, and nothing changes until you type YES.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-base " \fIPATH\fR"
Base path for relative entries (else the file's base: line, else the current directory
after you confirm).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIFORMAT\fR"
auto (default), lines or comma.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep\-folders
Empty the directories but leave the empty folders in place.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Validate and report only; change nothing.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-force
Skip the YES confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log " \fIPATH\fR"
Results CSV (default
.IR <inputfile>\-results\-<timestamp>.csv ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show its own help.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Bad arguments, nothing to do, or cancelled.
.TP
.B 2
The check ran but the answer was negative (port closed, reboot pending, duplicates found,
items skipped).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/
User install of the commands.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/
System install of the commands.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cli-tools/
.TQ
.I /usr/local/share/cli-tools/
README, per-tool docs, VERSION.txt and the list of installed files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR which (1),
.BR du (1),
.BR sha256sum (1),
.BR dig (1),
.BR openssl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/adam110th/cli-tools
